---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Kit-Bin | Free Browser-Based File Tools"
  description="Kit-Bin is a free collection of PDF, image, audio, video, and data tools that run entirely in your browser. No accounts, no uploads, no installs."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-ink dark:text-slate-100">About Kit-Bin</h1>
    <div class="text-ink dark:text-slate-300 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Kit-Bin is a collection of free, private, browser-based file tools, PDF, image, audio,
        video, and data, that run entirely on your device. There's no server involved in the
        actual conversion work; your device does it, using WebAssembly and native browser APIs,
        so the file you select never needs to leave it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's a deliberate choice, not a marketing line. See{' '}
        <a href="/guides/how-kit-bin-works/" class="text-primary dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline"
          >how Kit-Bin actually works</a
        >{' '}
        for the technical explanation, including how to verify it yourself using your browser's
        own developer tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is free to use, with no account required, and there is no subscription. Kit-Bin
        displays a small number of banner advertisements to help cover hosting and development
        costs, only if you accept them in the cookie banner shown on your first visit — see{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/#advertising" class="text-primary dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">how advertising works here</a>{' '}
        for the full details. If a tool has genuinely helped you, there's a{' '}
        <a href="/contact/" class="text-primary dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">contact page</a>{' '}
        and a way to support the site directly in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin also publishes a small set of{' '}
        <a href="/guides/" class="text-primary dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">guides</a>{' '}
        explaining the file formats and mechanics behind the tools, why iPhone photos won't open
        on Windows, why a PDF is larger than it looks, why a video can sound quiet even at full
        volume, for anyone who wants the actual explanation, not just the conversion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
